  "content": {
    "id": "p33-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "The polynomial $P(x)=x^3-4x^2+5x-1$ has roots $p$, $q$ and $r$. Find a polynomial $Q(x)$ with integer coefficients whose roots are $pq$, $qr$ and $rp$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": {
        "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
        "version": 1,
        "blocks": [
          {
            "id": "p33-q6-short-result",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "math",
                "latex": "Q(x)=x^3-5x^2+4x-1",
                "display": false
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "id": "p33-q6-short-method",
            "type": "paragraph",
            "fontSize": null,
            "align": "left",
            "spaceBefore": 0,
            "spaceAfter": 2,
            "lineHeight": 1.4,
            "indent": 0,
            "inlines": [
              {
                "type": "text",
                "text": "Use Vieta’s formulas to find the sum, pairwise-product sum and product of the new roots.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "By Vieta’s formulas,\n$$\\begin{align*}p+q+r&=4,\\\\pq+qr+rp&=5,\\\\pqr&=1.\\end{align*}$$\nFor the new roots,\n$$\\begin{align*}pq+qr+rp&=5,\\\\(pq)(qr)+(qr)(rp)+(rp)(pq)&=pqr(p+q+r),\\\\(pq)(qr)+(qr)(rp)+(rp)(pq)&=1\\times4,\\\\(pq)(qr)+(qr)(rp)+(rp)(pq)&=4,\\\\(pq)(qr)(rp)&=(pqr)^2,\\\\(pq)(qr)(rp)&=1.\\end{align*}$$\nTherefore, a suitable monic polynomial is\n$$\\begin{align*}Q(x)&=x^3-5x^2+4x-1.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 72
  },
